From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joseph Telaak <joseph@telaak.dev>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 00:09:14 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] sf_smac: read factory calibration from nvmem cells

The per-unit tx-power and XO calibration lives in the factory partition
at 0x800. The vendor kernel read it through its own sfax8_factory_read
module, which the open release does not ship, so the code that uses it
was compiled out and every board fell back to the generic tables. On
the Banana Pi BPI-WiFi5 that was measured as about 32 dB low on 2.4 GHz
and 11 dB low on 5 GHz.

Provide sf_get_value_from_factory() in the RF module instead, reading
nvmem cells on the "siflower,sf19a2890-rf" node: "calibration" for the
block at 0x800 (version tag, XO trim, tables) and an optional
"cooling-temp". The cells are looked up on demand, so the MAC driver
does not depend on the RF device having probed. The MAC addresses keep
coming from each MAC node's "mac-address" cell.

The header keeps the vendor's name and interface, so the call sites do
not change, and the driver now always builds with
CONFIG_SFAX8_FACTORY_READ.

Not compile-tested.

Signed-off-by: Joseph Telaak <joseph@telaak.dev>
